'''Mass Production EVA''' (エヴァ量産機, ''Eva Ryōsanki'', '''Mass Production EVA Unit''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Mass Production EVA
|image = E 740.png
|appearance = [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]
|money drop = 1,800¢ - 7,110¢
}}

==Enemy==
These secretly produced EVAs are similar to the Cat unit versions, being backliners with decent damage who might Freeze your units occasionally, and, being Immune to Curse, their abilities cannot be shut down, nor could Waves damage them. However, they are fairly slow and also have a long attack cycle. Note that these mass produced monstrosities aren't Eva Angels, but Traitless enemies, meaning that trying to use Eva Angel killers like [[Asuka Langley (Super Rare Cat)|Plug Suit Asuka]] or [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-02]] will probably lead towards your Eva Angel Killers getting stabbed and dismembered by the Mass Production EVAs. On the other hand, they are vulnerable to anti-Traitless specialists that are arguably more accessible.

==Strategy==
True to form, it's pretty easy to kill one of these, but when there's all nine on screen it gets really annoying to chip them down. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with his Talents can easily chain a solo Mass Production EVA alongside possible assistance from anti-Traitless units like [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] or [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]]. If you fail to pull this off, you can always just abuse their lengthy TBA and use rushers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to slowly chip them down, or stall them with a bunch of meatshields while you use units who outrange them like [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]]; [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]] also works but it's risky because he only outranges the EVAs by 5 range. Worst comes to worst, you can always abuse their lack of actual immunities and chip them down with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] over time.

